# What never goes into the image.
#
# Two reasons to keep this tight: a smaller build context uploads faster and
# caches better, and — the one that matters — anything copied in is readable
# by anyone who can pull the image.

# Secrets. config/dev.env and config/prod.env hold database passwords, the JWT
# signing secret and IP_PEPPER. In production these arrive through env_file at
# run time, never baked in.
config/*.env
.env
.env.*

# Installed and built on the other side of the COPY, for the image's own
# platform. Copying the host's versions in would at best waste time and at
# worst ship native modules built for Windows.
node_modules
dist

# History and tooling the runtime has no use for.
.git
.gitignore
.github
.vscode
.idea

# Generated documents and their sources.
docs

# Local file uploads (LOCAL_STORAGE_DIR). Production stores to S3.
storage

# Test output and logs.
coverage
*.log
npm-debug.log*

# Editor and OS noise.
*.swp
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
